@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title SIMD crossover — measured admission rather than assumed width

rectangle "Scalar H13 control\nLLVM SSE2 auto-vectorization" as BASE #DBE4FF
rectangle "Candidate: 4-word AVX2 minimum" as FOUR #FFF3BF
rectangle "4 words\nUnion -2.92%\nIntersection -2.08% (noise)" as FOUR_EXACT #D3F9D8
rectangle "5 words\nUnion +12.75%\nIntersection +9.74%" as FIVE #FFE3E3
rectangle "Reject 4-word policy\none vector + tail is adverse" as REJECT #FFA8A8
rectangle "Candidate: 8-word AVX2 minimum" as EIGHT #FFF3BF
rectangle "511/512 bits\nabout 13–15% faster" as EIGHT_EXACT #D3F9D8
rectangle "513-bit tail\nwithin noise" as EIGHT_TAIL #FFE8CC
rectangle "767–769 bits\nabout 12–23% faster" as WIDER #D3F9D8
rectangle "Retain 8-word threshold" as KEEP #B2F2BB
rectangle "Subset predicate\nprofitable scalar early exit" as SUBSET #E5DBFF
rectangle "Keep subset scalar" as SUBSET_KEEP #B2F2BB

BASE --> FOUR : compare identical fixture
FOUR --> FOUR_EXACT : exact vector width
FOUR --> FIVE : one-word tail
FOUR_EXACT --> REJECT : positive case is insufficient
FIVE --> REJECT : falsifying case
BASE --> EIGHT : compare identical fixture
EIGHT --> EIGHT_EXACT
EIGHT --> EIGHT_TAIL
EIGHT --> WIDER
EIGHT_EXACT --> KEEP
EIGHT_TAIL --> KEEP
WIDER --> KEEP
BASE --> SUBSET : independent control
SUBSET --> SUBSET_KEEP

note bottom of KEEP
  The threshold is eight storage words
  (512 stored bits), not eight logical bits.
end note

legend right
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<#DBE4FF>| immutable control |
  |<#FFF3BF>| candidate policy |
  |<#D3F9D8>| supporting measurement |
  |<#FFE8CC>| neutral boundary |
  |<#FFE3E3>| adverse measurement |
  |<#FFA8A8>| rejected policy |
  |<#E5DBFF>| distinct early-exit operation |
  |<#B2F2BB>| retained decision |
endlegend
@enduml
